/F2 9 Tf 54 670 Td (ABSTRACT) Tj
/F1 8.5 Tf 0 -13 Td (Software dependency resolution is classically formulated as an NP-complete constraint satisfaction problem, typically) Tj
0 -11 Td (solved using backtracking heuristics or Boolean Satisfiability (SAT / CDCL) solvers. While sound, SAT-based resolvers suffer) Tj
0 -11 Td (from exponential search degradation on cyclic peer dependencies and deep transitive dependency trees. Simultaneously,) Tj
0 -11 Td (package manager execution time during cold network installations is heavily dominated by redundant filesystem I/O:) Tj
0 -11 Td (archives are fetched over HTTP, written to disk as .tgz files, decompressed to intermediate caches, and copied or linked) Tj
0 -11 Td (into node_modules across multiple disk passes. This paper presents Jhol, an open-source package manager written in Rust) Tj
0 -11 Td (that addresses both bottlenecks: (1) Topological Dependency Resolution (JAGR-Infinite), mapping SemVer intervals to) Tj
0 -11 Td (continuous stalks in a cellular sheaf and eliminating 60%-83% of variables via Wilsonian RG decimation in under 10 us;) Tj
0 -11 Td (and (2) FastStream SSDP, streaming and decompressing HTTP/2 packages directly into the content-addressed store in a) Tj
0 -11 Td (single physical disk write pass. Evaluation across 15 real-world applications shows 0.1ms warm replays, 17.0ms cached) Tj
0 -11 Td (installs, and 38.0ms cold resolutions at 6.7 MB peak RAM with 100% Node.js load parity.) Tj
